From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 05:45:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add CPU cooling to the thermal
 zones

The CPU thermal zones only have a critical trip, which powers the
system off, and nothing cools the CPUs before it. Add a passive trip at
90 degrees C with a hysteresis of 2 degrees to cpub-thermal and
cpul-thermal, poll them every 500 ms while it is active, and map it to
the cpufreq cooling device of the cluster the zone belongs to: cpu6 for
the Cortex-A76 cores, cpu0 for the Cortex-A55 cores. Both CPUs get a
cooling-cells property of 2, as the first CPU of a cluster owns the
cluster's cpufreq policy.

The zones of the DDR, the GPU and the NPU keep only their critical trip,
as nothing can cool them yet.

The trip is 25 degrees C under the 115 degrees C that the datasheet
allows for continuous operation, and 20 under the critical trip. The
temperature sensors are rated at 3 degrees C, so a reading of 90 means
at most 93.

Not covered: a trend filter. The step_wise governor acts on every raw
sample of the sensor.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; with the temperature of
the A76 zone forced above its passive trip, the cooling device of the
A76 cluster limits the cluster below its top rate and releases it when
the forced temperature is withdrawn (the A55 zone was not forced).

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 33 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index 5052e2369eb8..2035741da74b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #include <dt-bindings/reset/allwinner,sun60i-a733-ccu.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/reset/allwinner,sun60i-a733-r-ccu.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/reset/allwinner,sun60i-a733-serdes-ccu.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/thermal/thermal.h>
 
 / {
 	interrupt-parent = <&gic>;
@@ -64,6 +65,7 @@ cpu0: cpu@0 {
 			enable-method = "psci";
 			capacity-dmips-mhz = <454>;
 			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep_a55>;
+			#cooling-cells = <2>;
 			i-cache-size = <32768>;
 			i-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			i-cache-sets = <128>;
@@ -166,6 +168,7 @@ cpu6: cpu@600 {
 			enable-method = "psci";
 			capacity-dmips-mhz = <1024>;
 			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep_a76>;
+			#cooling-cells = <2>;
 			i-cache-size = <65536>;
 			i-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			i-cache-sets = <256>;
@@ -1082,32 +1085,58 @@ cpu_ccu: clock-controller@8870000 {
 	thermal-zones {
 		/* sensor 3 sits next to the Cortex-A76 cores */
 		cpub-thermal {
-			polling-delay-passive = <0>;
+			polling-delay-passive = <500>;
 			polling-delay = <1000>;
 			thermal-sensors = <&ths 3>;
 
 			trips {
+				cpub_passive: cpub-passive {
+					temperature = <90000>;
+					hysteresis = <2000>;
+					type = "passive";
+				};
+
 				cpub-crit {
 					temperature = <110000>;
 					hysteresis = <0>;
 					type = "critical";
 				};
 			};
+
+			cooling-maps {
+				map0 {
+					trip = <&cpub_passive>;
+					cooling-device = <&cpu6 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>;
+				};
+			};
 		};
 
 		/* sensor 0 sits next to the Cortex-A55 cores */
 		cpul-thermal {
-			polling-delay-passive = <0>;
+			polling-delay-passive = <500>;
 			polling-delay = <1000>;
 			thermal-sensors = <&ths 0>;
 
 			trips {
+				cpul_passive: cpul-passive {
+					temperature = <90000>;
+					hysteresis = <2000>;
+					type = "passive";
+				};
+
 				cpul-crit {
 					temperature = <110000>;
 					hysteresis = <0>;
 					type = "critical";
 				};
 			};
+
+			cooling-maps {
+				map0 {
+					trip = <&cpul_passive>;
+					cooling-device = <&cpu0 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>;
+				};
+			};
 		};
 
 		ddr-thermal {
